{%- comment -%}
  Section: siwa-tester-invite | Owner: A-07 | Task: ST-08

  Feature bible Section 8, and two Phase-P0 features in one surface:
  CCF-01 (the tester as a primary CTA) and CCF-07 (the Discovery Kit). It is
  the last thing on the homepage on purpose — a reader who has scrolled past
  the hero, two product rows, the story and the bento has one objection left,
  and it is trust gap 1: "I cannot smell it before I buy it." Gap 4 — "what
  if I hate it after buying full-size" — is the same objection with money
  attached. Both are answered by the same sentence: try it first.

  "PRIMARY" IS A CLAIM ABOUT PROMINENCE, NOT ABOUT BUTTON STYLING.
  CCF-01 is titled "The Tester as a Primary CTA" and every button spec in the
  bible renders it btn-secondary. DESIGN.md principle 7 settles it: the tester
  has EQUAL visual weight to the main action — same height, same type size,
  same footprint — and takes the outline treatment, never the gold fill,
  unless it is the only CTA on the surface. This surface carries two CTAs, so
  the tester is `--tester` and the Discovery Kit is `--secondary`. Those two
  classes are visually identical by design (DESIGN.md §3.1); they are kept
  apart so CI rule 18 can assert the tester was never dressed as gold.

  THERE IS NO GOLD IN THIS SECTION AT ALL.
  Principle 1 rations gold to one per fold, and the homepage spends it in the
  hero and again in the Oracle invite. Two equal-weight doors is the point of
  the composition, not a compromise: a customer who is offered one loud option
  and one quiet one has been told which one the house wants.

  THE PRICE IS READ OFF A REAL VARIANT. IT IS NEVER TYPED.
  `tester_product` is a product picker. The variant whose title matches the
  global `settings.tester_variant_title` wins; if no variant matches, the
  product's own `price_min` is used. The figure then goes through `money` and
  is interpolated into `tester.cta` and `tester.first_crossing`. A hardcoded
  price would be a lie the moment the merchant changes it in Shopify.

  WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE PRICE CANNOT BE RESOLVED — the CTA is hidden.
  If `settings.tester_enabled` is off, or no product is picked, there is no
  price to state, so the panel keeps its heading (`tester.tier_label`) and its
  line (`tester.no_demand`) and drops the button entirely. It never renders a
  CTA with a zero, an empty string, or a typed fallback in it. `no_demand`
  carries no price and is therefore always safe to show.

  THE COPY REGISTER IS THE BIBLE'S AND IT IS ALREADY IN THE LOCALE FILES.
  "Buy a tester" is not the sentence. `tester.cta` is "Try it first — 85 EGP",
  `tester.first_crossing` is "The first crossing — 85 EGP", `tester.no_demand`
  is "Not ready to commit? The oracle doesn't demand it." Each is seeded in
  English and Arabic. Every setting on this section falls back to its
  `sections.tester_invite.*` key when the merchant leaves it blank, so a blank
  field degrades to translated house copy rather than to nothing.

  THE PRICE IS INTERPOLATED AS A PLAIN STRING, NOT WRAPPED IN MARKUP.
  Shopify escapes interpolated values for any key that does not end in
  `_html`, and none of these do, so a `.siwa-numeric` span passed into `t`
  would render as visible tags. The house precedent — siwa-announcement-bar —
  passes the `money` output plainly, and this file follows it. The offer
  headings carry `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` so the figure still sets
  as a number.

  THE KIT COLLECTION IS EMPTY TODAY AND THE EMPTY STATE IS REAL.
  The audit found `gift-boxes` carries no products. DESIGN.md §7.2: an empty
  state without a next action is a dead end, so it links out to the full
  catalogue rather than back to the empty collection the CTA already points
  at. Product cards go through `snippets/siwa-product-card.liquid`, which
  stamps ORIGINAL or IMPRESSION on every thumbnail (non-negotiable 1), and
  this section loads `assets/siwa-product-card.css` because that snippet's
  badge stack lives there.

  THE RHYTHM STAYS A CLASS — Gate 0 finding F2.
  `.siwa-section` / `.siwa-section--tight` halve themselves under 768px inside
  siwa-base.css. Emitting the rhythm as `#shopify-section-… { padding-block }`
  would outrank that media query and freeze the desktop rhythm at every
  viewport, which is exactly the trap the footer's column count fell into. So
  the rhythm is applied as a class and the two scoped declarations that DO
  need overriding — the merchant's extra padding and the kit's column count —
  are each emitted inside a media query that matches the one that overrides
  them.

  No JavaScript. Every control here is a link.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'siwa-tester-invite.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign heading_id = 'siwa-tester-invite-heading-' | append: section.id

  comment
    Setting blank falls back to the locale key. The merchant overrides the
    house sentence per section; they never have to retype it to keep it.
  endcomment
  assign eyebrow = 'sections.tester_invite.eyebrow' | t
  if s.eyebrow != blank
    assign eyebrow = s.eyebrow
  endif

  assign heading = 'sections.tester_invite.heading' | t
  if s.heading != blank
    assign heading = s.heading
  endif

  assign body = 'sections.tester_invite.body' | t
  if s.body != blank
    assign body = s.body
  endif

  assign kit_heading = 'sections.tester_invite.kit_heading' | t
  if s.kit_heading != blank
    assign kit_heading = s.kit_heading
  endif

  assign kit_body = 'sections.tester_invite.kit_body' | t
  if s.kit_body != blank
    assign kit_body = s.kit_body
  endif

  assign kit_cta_label = 'sections.tester_invite.kit_cta' | t
  if s.kit_cta_label != blank
    assign kit_cta_label = s.kit_cta_label
  endif

  comment
    THE TESTER PRICE, RESOLVED LIVE.
    Order: the variant named by settings.tester_variant_title, then the
    product's own price_min. `tester_ready` is a separate flag rather than a
    price test, because a legitimately free tester would read as "unresolved"
    if zero were the sentinel.
  endcomment
  assign tester_product = s.tester_product
  assign tester_ready = false
  assign tester_price = 0
  assign tester_href = ''

  if settings.tester_enabled and tester_product != blank
    assign wanted = settings.tester_variant_title | downcase | strip
    for variant in tester_product.variants
      assign candidate = variant.title | downcase | strip
      if wanted != blank and candidate == wanted
        assign tester_ready = true
        assign tester_price = variant.price
        assign tester_href = variant.url
        break
      endif
    endfor

    unless tester_ready
      assign tester_ready = true
      assign tester_price = tester_product.price_min
      assign tester_href = tester_product.url
    endunless

    if s.tester_url != blank
      assign tester_href = s.tester_url
    endif
  endif

  assign tester_money = tester_price | money
  assign tester_title = 'tester.tier_label' | t
  if tester_ready
    assign tester_title = 'tester.first_crossing' | t: price: tester_money
  endif
  assign tester_label = 'tester.cta' | t: price: tester_money
  assign tester_note = 'tester.no_demand' | t

  comment
    THE DISCOVERY KIT. The CTA points at the merchant's own URL first, then
    at the picked collection. With neither, the button is not rendered — a
    control that goes nowhere is worse than no control.
  endcomment
  assign kit = s.kit_collection
  assign kit_href = s.kit_url
  if kit_href == blank and kit != blank
    assign kit_href = kit.url
  endif

  assign show_kit_grid = false
  assign show_kit_empty = false
  if s.show_kit_products
    if kit != blank and kit.all_products_count > 0
      assign show_kit_grid = true
    else
      assign show_kit_empty = true
    endif
  endif
  assign empty_label = 'sections.product_row.empty_action' | t

  comment
    Media. The alt falls back to the image's own alt in the media library and
    then to the resolved heading, so it is never an English literal.
  endcomment
  assign image_alt = s.image_alt
  if image_alt == blank
    assign image_alt = s.image.alt
  endif
  if image_alt == blank
    assign image_alt = heading
  endif

  assign row_modifier = ''
  if s.media_position == 'inline-end'
    assign row_modifier = ' siwa-feature-row--reverse'
  endif

  comment
    Ground. `dark` reuses the design system's own .on-dark band, which each
    design direction re-points in assets/siwa-themes.css. No palette is
    invented here and no colour is authored.
  endcomment
  assign ground_class = 'siwa-tester-invite__band--' | append: s.color_scheme
  if s.color_scheme == 'dark'
    assign ground_class = ground_class | append: ' on-dark'
  endif

  assign rhythm_class = 'siwa-section'
  if s.rhythm == 'tight'
    assign rhythm_class = 'siwa-section--tight'
  endif
-%}

{%- if s.show_kit_products -%}
  {{ 'siwa-product-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}

{% style %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Extra padding only. The section's rhythm is the class on the inner
    container, so siwa-base.css keeps its own mobile step — finding F2.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-tester-invite__band {
    padding-block-start: {{ s.padding_top }}px;
    padding-block-end: {{ s.padding_bottom }}px;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Emitted inside a min-width query on purpose. A bare
    `#shopify-section-… { --siwa-kit-cols }` rule would outrank the two-column
    rule in assets/siwa-tester-invite.css and freeze the merchant's desktop
    column count on a 375px phone. Finding F2 again, same shape.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media (min-width: 769px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-tester-invite__kit-grid {
      --siwa-kit-cols: {{ s.kit_product_limit }};
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-tester-invite__band {
      padding-block-start: {{ s.mobile_padding_top }}px;
      padding-block-end: {{ s.mobile_padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<section class="siwa-tester-invite__band {{ ground_class }}" aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}">
  <div class="siwa-container siwa-tester-invite__inner {{ rhythm_class }}">
    <div class="siwa-feature-row{{ row_modifier }}">
      <div class="siwa-feature-row__media siwa-tester-invite__media">
        {%- if s.image != blank -%}
          {{
            s.image
            | image_url: width: 1200
            | image_tag:
              alt: image_alt,
              loading: 'lazy',
              widths: '400, 600, 800, 1200',
              sizes: '(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 560px'
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ 'lifestyle-2' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="siwa-feature-row__body siwa-tester-invite__body">
        <p class="siwa-label siwa-tester-invite__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
        <h2 class="siwa-h2 siwa-tester-invite__heading" id="{{ heading_id }}">{{ heading }}</h2>
        <div class="siwa-prose siwa-tester-invite__text">{{ body }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Two offers, one grid of equal columns, both CTAs pinned to the block-end
      of their panel. Principle 7's "same footprint" is a geometric claim, so
      it is met geometrically: equal columns, one shared button rule, buttons
      at 100% of their column.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="siwa-tester-invite__offers">
      <div class="siwa-tester-invite__offer siwa-tester-invite__offer--tester">
        <h3 class="siwa-h3 siwa-tester-invite__offer-title">{{ tester_title }}</h3>
        <p class="siwa-tester-invite__offer-body siwa-muted">{{ tester_note }}</p>

        {%- if tester_ready and tester_href != blank -%}
          <div class="siwa-tester-invite__actions">
            {%- render 'siwa-button', label: tester_label, href: tester_href, variant: 'tester' -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="siwa-tester-invite__offer siwa-tester-invite__offer--kit">
        <h3 class="siwa-h3 siwa-tester-invite__offer-title">{{ kit_heading }}</h3>
        <p class="siwa-tester-invite__offer-body siwa-muted">{{ kit_body }}</p>

        {%- if kit_href != blank -%}
          <div class="siwa-tester-invite__actions">
            {%- render 'siwa-button', label: kit_cta_label, href: kit_href, variant: 'secondary' -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if show_kit_grid -%}
      <div class="siwa-tester-invite__kit-grid">
        {%- for kit_product in kit.products limit: s.kit_product_limit -%}
          {%- render 'siwa-product-card',
            product: kit_product,
            heading_level: 'h4',
            show_inspired_by: false
          -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- elsif show_kit_empty -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A real empty state, because `gift-boxes` is empty today. It links to
        the whole catalogue rather than to the kit collection the CTA above
        already points at — sending someone from an empty shelf to the same
        empty shelf is not a next action.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="siwa-empty siwa-tester-invite__empty">
        <p>{{ 'sections.product_row.empty' | t }}</p>
        {%- render 'siwa-button',
          label: empty_label,
          href: routes.all_products_collection_url,
          variant: 'quiet'
        -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="siwa-trust siwa-tester-invite__trust" role="list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
            <li class="siwa-trust__item" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {{- block.settings.text -}}
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Tester invite",
  "class": "siwa-tester-invite",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated line for this section."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated line. Concise and confident — DESIGN.md §7.1."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated line. Say what the tester is and how long it lasts, not that it is small."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "The tester"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Principle 7 — the tester carries the same height, type size and footprint as the other action here, and takes the outline treatment rather than the gold fill. Its price is read live from the product you pick and is never typed into this section."
    },
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "tester_product",
      "label": "Tester product",
      "info": "The price shown comes from this product's tester variant, matched against Theme settings → Commerce → Tester variant title. With no matching variant the product's lowest price is used. With no product at all the CTA is hidden and the reassurance line stands on its own."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "tester_url",
      "label": "Tester link",
      "info": "Leave blank to link to the tester variant on its own product page."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "The Discovery Kit"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kit_heading",
      "label": "Kit heading",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated line."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kit_body",
      "label": "Kit body",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated line."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kit_cta_label",
      "label": "Kit button label",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the store's translated line. Keep it to a few words — the button is a single line and never wraps."
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "kit_collection",
      "label": "Kit collection",
      "info": "Used for the button's destination and, if you show them, for the products below."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "kit_url",
      "label": "Kit link",
      "info": "Leave blank to link to the collection above. With neither, the button is hidden rather than rendered dead."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_kit_products",
      "label": "Show the kit's products",
      "info": "Each thumbnail is stamped ORIGINAL or IMPRESSION. A collection with nothing in it shows a way out to the full catalogue instead.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "kit_product_limit",
      "label": "Products to show",
      "info": "Desktop only. The row falls to two across below 769px on its own.",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Media"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Image",
      "info": "Real product or workshop photography — anti-pattern 15. Blank shows a placeholder."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "image_alt",
      "label": "Image alt text",
      "info": "Describe the shot, not the brand: \"A tester vial beside its full bottle on stone\". Falls back to the alt set in your media library, then to the heading."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_position",
      "label": "Media position",
      "info": "Follows the reader's direction — start is the left in English and the right in Arabic.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inline-start", "label": "Start of the row" },
        { "value": "inline-end", "label": "End of the row" }
      ],
      "default": "inline-start"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout & spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "rhythm",
      "label": "Vertical rhythm",
      "info": "Ceremonial for a closing banner, tight next to a product row. DESIGN.md §4 asks that no two ceremonial blocks sit next to each other.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "section", "label": "Ceremonial" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" }
      ],
      "default": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Ground",
      "info": "Ink inverts the band through the design system's .on-dark tokens, which every design direction supplies. No colours are set on this section.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page", "label": "Page — the page ground" },
        { "value": "surface", "label": "Sand — one step up from the page" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink — inverted band" }
      ],
      "default": "surface"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top",
      "info": "Added to the vertical rhythm above, which already carries the section's own spacing.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 144,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "reassurance",
      "name": "Reassurance",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "One short factual line — what is sealed, what ships free, what you take at the door. A claim you cannot keep is worse than no claim (DESIGN.md §7.1)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Line"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Tester invite",
      "settings": {
        "rhythm": "section",
        "color_scheme": "surface",
        "media_position": "inline-start",
        "show_kit_products": false,
        "kit_product_limit": 3
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
